                            <a class="card-link collapsed" data-toggle="collapse" href="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="true">
                                <span>1</span> What is pressure washing, and how does it work?
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div id="collapseOne" class="collapse show" data-parent="#accordion">
                            <div class="card-body">
Pressure washing involves using high-pressure water spray to remove dirt, grime, mold, mildew, and other contaminants from surfaces like driveways, patios, decks, and exterior walls. The powerful stream of water can effectively clean and restore surfaces without the need for harsh chemicals, making it an eco-friendly cleaning option.

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header">
                            <a class="card-link" data-toggle="collapse" href="#collapseTwo">
                                <span>2</span> Is pressure washing safe for all surfaces?
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div id="collapseTwo" class="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">
                            <div class="card-body">
While pressure washing is effective for many surfaces, it's not suitable for all. Delicate surfaces like painted wood, some types of siding, and certain roofing materials can be damaged by high-pressure water. Our professionals assess each surface and adjust the pressure and technique to ensure safe and effective cleaning.

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header">
                            <a class="card-link" data-toggle="collapse" href="#collapseThree">
                                <span>3</span> How often should I get my surfaces pressure washed?
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div id="collapseThree" class="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">
                            <div class="card-body">
The frequency of pressure washing depends on various factors, including the type of surface, local climate, and exposure to elements. Generally, most homeowners benefit from pressure washing their exterior surfaces once a year. However, high-traffic areas or regions with heavy pollution or severe weather may require more frequent cleaning.

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header">
                            <a class="card-link" data-toggle="collapse" href="#collapseFour">
                                <span>4</span> Do I need to prepare my home or property before a pressure washing service?

                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div id="collapseFour" class="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">
                            <div class="card-body">
Yes, a few preparations can help ensure a smooth pressure washing service. Clear the area of any obstacles like furniture, vehicles, or decorations. Close all windows and doors tightly to prevent water from entering your home. Our team will take care of the rest, including protecting sensitive areas and plants.

                            </div>
                        </div>
